# Copy effects apply in timestamp order (CR 613.2a, 613.7), and one ending leaves the later ones (CR 611.2b). Bot1's Thespian's
# Stage is a copy of Mutavault "except it has this ability"; animated, it is a creature, and Mirrorweave targets it: Bot1's
# Ornithopter becomes a copy of it until end of turn - an unanimated Mutavault with the Stage's copy ability (CR 707.9b), a
# land and no creature. That Ornithopter-Mutavault then uses the copy ability to become a copy of Bot1's Plains, with no
# duration (a later timestamp). As the turn ends Mirrorweave's effect ends, and the Stage's later one is still there: on turn 6
# the Ornithopter is a Plains, not an Ornithopter.

[Bot1 Deck]
Thespian's Stage
Sol Ring
Ornithopter
Black Lotus
Mutavault
Plains
Forest
Mirrorweave
Forest x8

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x15

